 "content": "# Continual-ARC observation: framed seed creates nested square bands\n\nObserved in task-78feb3d5 (three input/output pairs, including one held-out solved correctly): A rectangular color-3 outline encloses a rectangular zero-filled cavity with one interior color-3 seed. Preserve the outer frame and all cells outside it. For each cavity cell, compute Chebyshev distance `d = max(abs(row-seed_row), abs(col-seed_col))` using cavity-relative or grid coordinates. Keep the seed (`d=0`) as 3; recolor cavity cells at positive odd distance to 4 and positive even distance to 2. This makes concentric axis-aligned square bands clipped by the cavity boundaries. Validate seed location and cavity bounds from each input; the seed need not be centered. Evidence: all three demos and the held-out test matched this rule; the held-out instance was accepted.\n"
